498
00:18:43,297 --> 00:18:45,073
A fire forced a move.

499
00:18:45,253 --> 00:18:47,853
A closing base provided the space.

500
00:18:48,033 --> 00:18:49,961
A squadron gave a symbol.

501
00:18:50,141 --> 00:18:52,003
None of that was in a business

502
00:18:52,003 --> 00:18:52,997
plan we can see.

503
00:18:53,177 --> 00:18:55,119
What the company did next,

504
00:18:55,119 --> 00:18:57,436
build faster and stranger cars,

505
00:18:57,436 --> 00:19:00,126
is documented, and we have shown the

506
00:19:00,126 --> 00:19:00,723
numbers.

507
00:19:01,073 --> 00:19:03,348
So why a fighter-jet hangar?

508
00:19:03,528 --> 00:19:06,073
The sources give a chain of events,

509
00:19:06,073 --> 00:19:07,673
not a stated strategy.

510
00:19:07,853 --> 00:19:10,489
A fire destroyed the old factory.

511
00:19:10,669 --> 00:19:13,153
A nearby base had just closed.

512
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:14,749
The company moved in.

513
00:19:14,929 --> 00:19:17,548
Nowhere in our sources does Christian von

514
00:19:17,548 --> 00:19:20,229
Koenigsegg say the hangar was a deliberate

515
00:19:20,229 --> 00:19:22,273
choice, and none of them gives a

516
00:19:22,273 --> 00:19:23,741
rent or purchase price.

517
00:19:23,921 --> 00:19:25,907
The answer is circumstance.

518
00:19:26,257 --> 00:19:29,158
There are practical reasons a hangar could

519
00:19:29,158 --> 00:19:30,264
suit a carmaker,

520
00:19:30,264 --> 00:19:32,406
such as large open floors and a

521
00:19:32,406 --> 00:19:34,686
doorway wide enough for aircraft.

522
00:19:34,866 --> 00:19:36,309
That is our inference,

523
00:19:36,309 --> 00:19:37,885
not a documented reason,

524
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:39,985
and none of our sources list the

525
00:19:39,985 --> 00:19:41,298
hangar's dimensions.

526
00:19:41,478 --> 00:19:43,506
We mention it only because a reader

527
00:19:43,506 --> 00:19:45,244
will wonder, and we want to be

528
00:19:45,244 --> 00:19:47,331
clear about which parts are fact and

529
00:19:47,331 --> 00:19:48,374
which are guesses.

530
00:19:48,724 --> 00:19:50,055
The tribute side,

531
00:19:50,055 --> 00:19:51,777
though, is documented.

532
00:19:51,957 --> 00:19:54,937
Wikipedia says the ghost symbol was adopted

533
00:19:54,937 --> 00:19:56,946
as a tribute to the squadron,

534
00:19:56,946 --> 00:20:00,133
and SlashGear says the pilots themselves asked

535
00:20:00,133 --> 00:20:00,618
for it.

536
00:20:00,798 --> 00:20:02,786
That is a human detail in a

537
00:20:02,786 --> 00:20:03,817
story of fire,

538
00:20:03,817 --> 00:20:05,364
closures and finance:

539
00:20:05,364 --> 00:20:08,015
a group of airmen losing their base,

540
00:20:08,015 --> 00:20:11,108
and a carmaker keeping their emblem alive.

541
00:20:11,458 --> 00:20:12,491
What is missing.

542
00:20:12,671 --> 00:20:14,378
The cause of the fire.

543
00:20:14,558 --> 00:20:16,264
The size of the hangar.

544
00:20:16,444 --> 00:20:18,685
What the lease or purchase cost.

545
00:20:18,865 --> 00:20:21,802
Whether the CC8S reached Geneva on time.

546
00:20:21,982 --> 00:20:24,712
Whether the original hangar is still used

547
00:20:24,712 --> 00:20:27,242
after the twenty twenty-three factory.

548
00:20:27,422 --> 00:20:29,852
And the founder's own account of why

549
00:20:29,852 --> 00:20:31,067
he chose the base.

550
00:20:31,247 --> 00:20:33,291
If you have a primary source for

551
00:20:33,291 --> 00:20:34,121
any of these,

552
00:20:34,121 --> 00:20:35,589
put it in the comments.

553
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:36,800
So a fire,

554
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:39,296
a closed air base and a ghost

555
00:20:39,296 --> 00:20:42,824
squadron produced one of the world's more

556
00:20:42,824 --> 00:20:44,717
unusual car factories.

557
00:20:44,897 --> 00:20:46,479
We can document the dates,

558
00:20:46,479 --> 00:20:48,244
